@politics

= Inter-party Relations

**{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Democratic Party" style="color: #0015bc;">Democrats</span>!}**: [+ dem_relation : relationships +]

[? if liberal_split = 1 : **{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Liberal Republican Party" style="color: #DAA520;">Lib. Rep.</span>!}**: [+ liberal_relation : relationships +] ?]

= Internal Factions of the Party

**{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="The Radicals support total equality for the freedmen and believe in retribution" style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radical</span>!}** strength: [+ radical_strength : strength +], dissent: [+ radical_dissent : dissent +]

**{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="The Moderates follow the ideas of Lincoln and quick reintegration of the south" style="color: #9D2933;">Moderate</span>!}** strength: [+ moderate_strength : strength +], dissent: [+ moderate_dissent : dissent +]

**{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Oppose the more ideas of the Radical Republicans and sought a less extreme path for southern reintegration" style="color: #B5651D;">Conservative</span>!}** strength: [+ conservative_strength : strength +], dissent: [+ conservative_dissent : dissent +]

[? if liberal_split = 0 : **{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Support civil liberties and free markets, but are skeptical of strong federal enforcement of racial equality or occupation policies" style="color: #DAA520;">Liberal</span>!}** strength: [+ liberal_strength : strength +], dissent: [+ liberal_dissent : dissent +] ?]

[? if liberal_split = 1 : The Liberal faction has broken away to form the Liberal Republican Party. ?]

